		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4815&amp;p=35596#p35596"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>The specs are quite clear.<br>It sends YOUR Tx frequency, the CSS (CTCSS or DCS), the shift.<br>The CSS letter could also be a 'T' (with 'off''). The case of the letter describe if bandwidth (upcase for 25kHz, lowcase for 12.5).<br>On the TH-D74, you have a "Tune" option when you browse the received beacons, that will do a QSY to that given frequency, with correct shift and tone.<br>Of course, here, there's a limit of the sent parameters to what the transceiver supports (and in case you are on a 1750Hz one, that tone is not sent in the beacon), range is also not supported, etc.</div></blockquote>Take a look on this video, 145.230 is the  output frequency on the repeater and it has a - 0.600 shift.<br><br><a href="https://youtu.be/sUuJf4-N_cw?si=qVrw2xH9m3dCFbHE&amp;t=256" class="postlink">https://youtu.be/sUuJf4-N_cw?si=qVrw2xH9m3dCFbHE&amp;t=256</a> <br><br>Similar with the other examples.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Wed Feb 05, 2025 10:07 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
