		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4815&amp;p=35590#p35590"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><ul><li> Fix firmware freezing when an APRS becon can't be sent (like when the squelch is constantly opened).</li></ul>The firmwares are available at: <a href="https://drive.proton.me/urls/VRT4Q1YYAG#q28Sr1aVBTQg" class="postlink">https://drive.proton.me/urls/VRT4Q1YYAG#q28Sr1aVBTQg</a><br>The voice prompts are available at: <a href="https://drive.proton.me/urls/H0XNJZFH08#YPSZxRlhHBGG" class="postlink">https://drive.proton.me/urls/H0XNJZFH08#YPSZxRlhHBGG</a><br><br><strong class="text-strong">NOTE</strong>: You <span style="text-decoration:underline">need</span> to use a CPS version greater or equal the the 2025/01/26. See the CPS section <a href="https://www.opengd77.com/viewtopic.php?f=12&amp;t=4804" class="postlink">viewtopic.php?f=12&amp;t=4804</a><br><br>For translators, the on-screen texts, voice prompts CSV and CPS XML files are located at: <a href="https://drive.proton.me/urls/256SP2W1NM#mC9d2L32MEmb" class="postlink">https://drive.proton.me/urls/256SP2W1NM#mC9d2L32MEmb</a></div></blockquote>Regarding the QSY info, I'm a bit confused if it shows the correct info , I tried to study the more "official" links:<br><a href="http://www.aprs.org/info/freqspec.txt" class="postlink">http://www.aprs.org/info/freqspec.txt</a><br><a href="http://aprsisce.wikidot.com/doc:qsy" class="postlink">http://aprsisce.wikidot.com/doc:qsy</a><br><br>But it's a still a bit unclear for me if you should announce the downlink ( Repeater TX ) or uplink ( Repeater RX ) <br><br>My MD9600 seems to announce the uplink ( My radios TX freq) on a repeater channel:<br><br>2025-02-03 22:18:06 CET: SA0BUX-9&gt;APOG77,WIDE1-1,WIDE2-1,qAR,SM0RGQ-4:!\0Ou)S%VbC  !432.625MHz c077 +200 OpenGD77 MD-9600<br>2025-02-03 22:19:43 CET: SA0BUX-9&gt;APOG77,WIDE1-1,WIDE2-1,qAO,SK0CT-1:!\0Ou3S%VNC  !145.187MHz toff +060 OpenGD77 MD-9600</div></blockquote>I have pooked around and tried to understand how it works on various Kenwood radios and it seems that they send the repeaters output frequency together with the shift. <br>Here we have it the other way around. <br><br>Problem is that the "specifications" don't clearly define how it should work.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Wed Feb 05, 2025 6:40 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
